# Planning Docs

## PRD

Write PRDs to `docs/prd/<feature>.md` with: Problem, Users, User Stories, Non-Goals, Success Metrics, and Open Questions.

User stories must include P0, P1, or P2 priority and testable Given/When/Then acceptance criteria.

## Architecture

Write architecture docs to `docs/architecture/<feature>.md` with: Overview, API Contracts, Data Model, Module Boundaries, Async Jobs, Caching, and ADRs.

Shared contracts go in `packages/shared` before frontend and backend implementation begin in parallel.

## Design

Write screen specs to `docs/design/<feature>.md` when UI changes. Map every screen to `packages/ui` components and include empty, loading, error, success, and responsive states.

## Documentation Governance

- Keep entrypoints short: `README.md` for human startup, `docs/PRODUCT.md` for current product state, and `docs/execution/README.md` for workflow navigation.
- Use one canonical source per topic. Link to canonical docs instead of repeating long sections.
- Mark stale docs as superseded and move historical content to `docs/archive/` instead of deleting useful context.
- If the user requests direct deletion of old docs, first update or remove active references, then delete the stale file instead of leaving a pointer-only document.
- Feature docs should be read on demand: `docs/prd/<feature>.md`, `docs/architecture/<feature>.md`, and `docs/design/<feature>.md`.
- After renaming or deleting rules/docs, search active docs and agents for stale references.
